 ## Unreleased
 
+- speech: Drama requests accept `temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k` (1 through 64) and exact unsigned 64-bit `seed`. Whole replies, streams, references, guidance and long-form segments retain the requested settings; omitted or null fields keep existing defaults. Explicit seeds advance by each segment's attempt number on redraws. See [speech sampling](docs/speech-sampling.md).
+
 - speech: long-form Drama 3 splits preserve complete special tokens, bracketed cues and nested paired direction tags, even when one span exceeds the character target. CJK punctuation supplies sentence and clause boundaries without requiring spaces, and topic-shift markers inside protected spans cannot split them. Existing input, prompt-token, segment and frame limits still apply ([docs](docs/drama-voices.md#long-form-replies)).
 - speech: Drama 3's DAC activation planes are bounded by the decode chunk and causal halo rather than the utterance limit. QKV history retains absolute frame indexing and attention tile boundaries. `zig build drama-codec-chunk` builds `oracle/bin/tf-drama-codec-chunk CHECKPOINT`, a GPU byte-equality gate against the original full-plane layout; the trace diagnostic explicitly retains that reference layout.
 - speech: `--silence-mid-s S` (CUDA; 0 for off, or 3 to below 10; default 0) ends a Drama 3 synthesis as `silence` when its end of speech comes inside S seconds or more below -40 dBFS after 1 s or more voiced: a reply that fell silent mid-way and stopped there, its last words never spoken, as one 4-bit take did after a 9.0 s hole. Holes that recover are left alone, since a client that shortens pauses never plays them, and a reply the frame cap stops is not judged. Such a draw is redrawn under the silence redraws' rules, a long-form segment in place, and whole replies count the draws it ended in `X-Silence-Mid-Trips`. Replayed at S = 3 over 2272 draws in the engine's frame accounting, it ended 15 of the 2047 that the 10 s rule left alone; all 8 with a text to judge by had lost words, and none of them had spoken in full. With S = 0 replies are as before ([docs](docs/drama-voices.md#holes-that-end-a-reply))
