+- **Seeds.** Without an explicit request seed, each segment's seed comes from its own prompt rows, as a single synthesis's does. An explicit seed starts each segment's attempt count at zero; its redraws use seed + attempt modulo 2^64. Every segment keeps the same requested temperature, top-p and top-k; see [speech sampling](speech-sampling.md).
 - **Limits.**
   - More than 12 segments are refused up front.
   - A reply may use 6000 frames in all; each segment gets at most what is left.
